# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Every text file is stored LF in the index (verified 2026-09-14: 2176/2176
# tracked text blobs were already i/lf, so adding this rewrites nothing).
# `text=auto` keeps it that way — a CRLF file can no longer be committed as CRLF.
* text=auto

# Files that are PARSED LINE-BY-LINE also get LF in the WORKING TREE.
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and what this machine has set) checks
# text files out as CRLF, so a repo-consistent index still produced a mixed working
# tree — prompts/adventure-guides.txt was CRLF while its four sibling guide files
# were LF. Header regexes anchored with `$` (e.g. /^\[([a-z0-9-]+)\]$/) then failed
# silently and all 15 adventure guides parsed as null on Windows only (parser fixed
# in 711ea7558; `eol=lf` removes the input that caused it).
*.txt text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
